      "impact": "An adopter who configures `scp/policy-check-readback` (a commit STATUS) as the required check — rather than `policy-check / scp/policy-check` (a check-RUN) — creates a gate bypassable by any runner with `statuses: write`. The distinction between the two context types is explained in D-033 and docs/security/branch-protection.md, but not in §12.7 where an adopter makes the branch-protection configuration decision.",
